<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armistice of Cherasco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Armistice of Cherasco was signed on 28 April 1796 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> of Victor Amadeus III, after a two-week French campaign in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>. It took the kingdom out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a> and handed key fortresses and free passage to the French. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1783">Treaty of Paris</a> that followed in May ceded Savoy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nice">Nice</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armistice-of-cherasco.jpg" alt="Armistice of Cherasco" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Etienne Pierre Motte (1785 - 1836) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armistizio_di_Cherasco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
